# Git remotes — use origin2 by default

This repo uses two remotes:

| Remote | URL | Use |
|--------|-----|-----|
| `origin` | `git@github-ca.corp.zynga.com:fgusmao/lab.git` | Corporate mirror; VPN required |
| `origin2` | `git@github.com:orchestrai-tools/orchestrai.git` | **Default for everything** |

GitHub repo for `gh` and PRs: **`orchestrai-tools/orchestrai`**

## Default policy

Treat **`origin2`** as the canonical remote for all git and GitHub work unless the user explicitly names `origin`.

Applies to:

- push, fetch, pull, rebase, merge-base diffs
- branch create/track/upstream
- pull requests (`gh pr create`, `gh pr view`, comments, checks)
- CI status and subscriptions
- comparing against base branch (`origin2/main`)

Do **not** use `origin` for any of the above by default.

## Push and branch tracking

- Always push to `origin2`.
- Set upstream on `origin2`: `git push -u origin2 <branch>`.
- If a branch still tracks `origin/*`, push to `origin2` and fix upstream before opening a PR.

```bash
# ✅ Default
git push -u origin2 HEAD
git fetch origin2
git pull origin2 main
git log origin2/main..HEAD
git diff origin2/main...HEAD

# ❌ Wrong unless the user asked for origin
git push origin main
git pull origin main
```

## Pull requests

Before `gh pr create`:

1. Push the branch to `origin2`.
2. Pass the repo explicitly so `gh` does not follow `origin`:

```bash
git push -u origin2 HEAD
gh pr create --repo orchestrai-tools/orchestrai --base main ...
```

For other GitHub commands, prefer `--repo orchestrai-tools/orchestrai`:

```bash
gh pr view --repo orchestrai-tools/orchestrai
gh pr checks --repo orchestrai-tools/orchestrai
gh run list --repo orchestrai-tools/orchestrai
```

## Force push

- Never force-push to `main` on either remote unless the user explicitly requests it.
- If they ask to force-push without naming a remote, use `origin2`.

## When to use origin

Only when the user explicitly asks to push, fetch, or sync with the corporate remote (`origin` / `fgusmao/lab` on Zynga GitHub).
